                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "cd4b3509-8b9b-4d26-85db-8d126268a151",
                        "entry_id": "85830873-806f-354c-95e1-ec53c870f0a0",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "spleets"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "c7c96c61-c2ba-31ad-918c-2fe0b12b9eb3",
                        "entry_id": "85830873-806f-354c-95e1-ec53c870f0a0",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A small strip of split wood or willow."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "countable",
                            "obsolete",
                            "uncountable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "d052e3ce-3a54-4562-ac7b-126025613259",
                                "sense_id": "c7c96c61-c2ba-31ad-918c-2fe0b12b9eb3",
                                "text": "But if the hiue be more then fourteene inches ouer within, it may wel receiue foure spleets."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "d61568d0-7a64-4c6c-a423-91c25f811f90",
                                "sense_id": "c7c96c61-c2ba-31ad-918c-2fe0b12b9eb3",
                                "text": "Your Hive being pruned put in your ſpleets, 3 or 4 of them, as the largeneſs of your hive ſhall require, the upper ends whereof ſet together at the top of the hive, and the lower faſten about a handful above the Skirt; beſides theſe ſpleets within the hive, the ſtraw hive muſt have 4 other ſpleets driven up into the Skirts to keep the hive from Sinking when it is Loaded, […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "6bd611cd-04e8-45a3-874d-0f053fa7af3e",
                                "sense_id": "c7c96c61-c2ba-31ad-918c-2fe0b12b9eb3",
                                "text": "[B]ind their ſtems together with a ſpleet of willow, or ſome tough wood, by wrapping it about them three or four times, and tucking the end under. […] a ſmall wreath, made of ſpleet, is ſlipped on the upper end of the ſtaff, which holds it together, and keeps the whole from falling about."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "abfa067c-583a-4fc2-8fa7-4ffd23ecfece",
                                "sense_id": "c7c96c61-c2ba-31ad-918c-2fe0b12b9eb3",
                                "text": "Spleets, or ſticks, are proper to ſupport the combs, when extended near the bottom; […] as the combs are uſually built in parallel lines from front to back, each comb, when wrought down, being of conſiderable weight, it will have a ready ſupport from the ſpleet, and which will ſerve to faſten them alſo; […]"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [],
                "word_linkages": []
            },
            {
